module io.files

--[[
Portable filesystem access accepts native paths on native hosts and
application-owned paths on browser hosts. Set an application identity before
resolving the portable configuration, data, or cache directory.

```nupp
local files = require("io.files")
files.setapplicationidentity("example", "notes")

local data = assert(files.datapath())
assert(files.write(data:join("notes.txt"), "hello"))
```

Native programs may also pass ordinary strings or [](io.path.Path)
values. Browser programs refuse raw path text and use the opaque
`ApplicationPath` values returned by `configurationpath`, `datapath`, or
`cachepath`.

Browser application data lives in the Origin Private File System. It remains
evictable unless `requestpersistentstorage` succeeds. Capability flags describe
the operations whose native semantics have no browser equivalent.
]]
